# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a throw inside a backward-branch loop hits a safepoint; the
#         pending_unwind check at safepoint runs urbi_unwind(); the catch
#         block absorbs the exception; execution continues after the try/catch.
#
# defer-to: T39
#
# Reason: while try/catch/throw are fully wired at M3 (T10) and the safepoint
# pending_unwind path is implemented, observing that the *safepoint* (not a
# direct throw at a non-loop site) triggers the unwind requires a construct
# where OP_THROW fires inside a loop body so that the backward-branch
# safepoint fires first.  This cannot be expressed cleanly in pure urbiscript
# at M3 without the tunables-header to set a tiny budget (otherwise the loop
# might not reach the safepoint before the throw).  T39 provides the tunables
# hook.
#
# Note: basic try/catch correctness (throw outside loops) is already tested
# in tests/chk/control_transfer/ (T13 fixtures) and unit tests (T9/T10).
# This fixture specifically targets the safepoint-then-unwind path.
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by:
#   ## tunables: URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX=2
#   try { var i = 0; while (i < 1) { i = i + 1; throw 99 } } catch (e) { echo(e) }
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 99
